tweets.text:
@aka_lacie "Jensen Huang is considering a comeback as Nvidia’s chief executive, as allies in Silicon Valley pressure the company’s board to reinstate him days after the tech executive resigned over reports he had affairs with a suspected Chinese spy and a subordinate. 

Huang has discussed with confidantes the possibility of returning, according to multiple people familiar with the matter — even as an independent probe by Nvidia’s board investigates the conduct that led to a spectacular leadership crisis at the $4tn chip company this week. 

One Huang ally told the FT they were putting together a “war room” of Silicon Valley executives to lobby for the former Nvidia chief’s return and would try to garner support from the White House."

@snmart Yeah, $IQE got backstopped by $MTSI and signed $TSEM agreements since I originally took positions!

Earnings saw revenue acceleration too from 30%->40% and margins increase.

Fundamentals keep improving despite share prices not reflecting it, but over medium/long horizon I think things keep improving

@invest_create Not even joking I heard a hedge fund manager the other day say

“I don’t like $INTC” not a fan of memory. 

Majority won’t understand the nuances

@AsgardArru I just find it interesting that everyone likes to use the Warren Buffett quote: "Be greedy when others are fearful"

But when a crash actually happens, everyone makes fun of folks like Morgan Stanley when they say "Maximum Overweight"

Not saying I agree with this positioning, but I just found their stance interesting enough to share.

